WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:17.485
"What?" Henry exclaimed, staring at Cole.

2
00:00:17.486 --> 00:00:23.463
"What do you mean, you put the lollipop in Daisy's pocket? Why?"

3
00:00:23.464 --> 00:00:25.813
Cole shrugged, looking sheepish.

4
00:00:25.814 --> 00:00:30.235
"I knew that Daisy loves those blueberry lollipops from the Dessert Den.

5
00:00:30.236 --> 00:00:34.305
She couldn't stop talking about them when I saw her there yesterday.

6
00:00:34.306 --> 00:00:40.072
So I decided to surprise her with one as a . . . um . . . good luck gift.

7
00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:43.989
I waited until she left to get some lemonade," he continued.

8
00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:48.809
"Then I sneaked into the barn and stuck a lollipop in the pocket of her show shirt."

9
00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:54.633
"You did?" Henry said. "Why? You didn't get Maggie anything.

10
00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:56.846
She likes candy too."

11
00:00:56.847 --> 00:01:02.767
"That's different." Cole looked embarrassed. "Maggie's just . . . Maggie.

12
00:01:02.768 --> 00:01:07.797
Daisy is, you know, really nice and pretty and smart."

13
00:01:07.798 --> 00:01:13.941
"Oh!" Henry thought. "Cole has a crush on Daisy!"

14
00:01:13.942 --> 00:01:18.201
"Is that why you skipped swim team practice today?" he asked.

15
00:01:18.202 --> 00:01:22.423
"Because of Daisy? You wanted to watch her compete?"

16
00:01:22.424 --> 00:01:27.449
"Maybe." Cole shrugged. "I mean, I wanted to help you guys too."

17
00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:32.097
"Okay," Henry said. "So what happened with the shirt?

18
00:01:32.098 --> 00:01:34.568
Did you leave it in the water trough?"

19
00:01:34.569 --> 00:01:40.065
"No!" Cole said. "I just put the lollipop in Daisy's shirt pocket.

20
00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:43.540
Then I left it hanging in the barn by Coco's stall."

21
00:01:43.541 --> 00:01:50.489
"When you said you were looking for more napkins, you were really hanging out with Daisy," Henry guessed.

22
00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:53.581
"That's when you put the lollipop in her pocket."

23
00:01:53.582 --> 00:01:58.567
Cole nodded. "I was going to tell Daisy later that the lollipop was from me.

24
00:01:58.568 --> 00:02:02.348
But then her shirt disappeared!" He sighed.

25
00:02:02.349 --> 00:02:05.166
"I was afraid someone saw me near her shirt.

26
00:02:05.167 --> 00:02:09.319
That person could tell Daisy—and make her think that I stole it!"

27
00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:15.235
Henry sighed. "Why didn't you just say so in the first place?"

28
00:02:15.236 --> 00:02:18.247
"I don't know." Cole looked sheepish again.

29
00:02:18.248 --> 00:02:20.828
"I thought I could find the shirt myself.

30
00:02:20.829 --> 00:02:24.456
That way nobody would ever know about the candy and stuff."

31
00:02:24.457 --> 00:02:29.668
Henry nodded. Now he understood why Cole had been acting so strange all day.

32
00:02:29.669 --> 00:02:34.977
The trouble was, Cole's explanation didn't explain what had happened to Daisy's shirt.

33
00:02:34.978 --> 00:02:40.121
"So you have no idea how the shirt got into the water trough?" he asked.

34
00:02:40.122 --> 00:02:42.274
"Nope." Cole shook his head.

35
00:02:42.275 --> 00:02:45.038
Normally Henry wouldn't doubt his best friend.

36
00:02:45.039 --> 00:02:47.812
But Cole had told a lot of lies today.

37
00:02:47.813 --> 00:02:50.775
Still, he wanted to trust his best friend.

38
00:02:50.776 --> 00:02:53.865
"Maybe it's a red herring," he muttered.

39
00:02:53.866 --> 00:02:56.055
"A what?" Cole said.

40
00:02:56.056 --> 00:02:58.681
"A red herring," Henry said.

41
00:02:58.682 --> 00:03:02.122
"That's something that seems like a clue, but isn't.

42
00:03:02.123 --> 00:03:06.480
Like that blue stain. Maybe it's just a coincidence.

43
00:03:06.481 --> 00:03:12.962
Maybe Rebecca—or someone else—grabbed the shirt without even noticing the lollipop in the pocket."

44
00:03:12.963 --> 00:03:15.696
"That makes sense," Cole agreed.

45
00:03:15.697 --> 00:03:18.270
Henry frowned as he kept thinking.

46
00:03:18.271 --> 00:03:22.254
"But in that case, what happened to the lollipop?

47
00:03:22.255 --> 00:03:25.219
It wasn't in the pocket when we found the shirt.

48
00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:28.430
And I didn't see it in the water trough."

49
00:03:28.431 --> 00:03:31.507
"Maybe a horse ate it," Cole suggested.

50
00:03:31.508 --> 00:03:34.851
Henry thought about Big Spot's blue slobber.

51
00:03:34.852 --> 00:03:43.647
"Maybe. But why would someone steal the shirt and then leave it in such an obvious place?" he asked.

52
00:03:43.648 --> 00:03:50.149
"If Rebecca was trying to ruin things for Daisy, Rebecca would have found a better hiding spot for the shirt.

53
00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:53.006
This just doesn't make sense."

54
00:03:53.007 --> 00:03:56.549
Henry had the feeling he was missing some important clue.

55
00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:59.179
But he couldn't figure out what it was.

56
00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:00.799
He glanced around.

57
00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:04.700
Everyone was gathering near the ring to watch the next class.

58
00:04:04.701 --> 00:04:07.471
There were no lemonade customers in sight.

59
00:04:07.472 --> 00:04:11.417
"Let's go check the scene of the crime again," he suggested.

60
00:04:11.418 --> 00:04:15.947
"Okay," Cole said. "Listen, I'm sorry I didn't tell you earlier.

61
00:04:15.948 --> 00:04:18.205
About the lollipop, I mean."

62
00:04:18.206 --> 00:04:23.637
"That's okay." Henry led the way toward the barn.

63
00:04:23.638 --> 00:04:28.649
When Henry and Cole entered, Cole went over to Maggie, who was near Big Spot's stall.

64
00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:32.822
Henry saw Coco in her stall, though Daisy was nowhere in sight.

65
00:04:32.823 --> 00:04:36.201
Instead Rebecca was standing there patting the pony.

66
00:04:36.202 --> 00:04:42.494
"Hi," said Henry. "Did you notice the clothes that were hanging on this stall earlier?"

67
00:04:42.495 --> 00:04:48.053
"Clothes?" Rebecca rubbed Coco's nose. "No. Why?"

68
00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:51.065
"There was a show shirt—" Henry began.

69
00:04:51.066 --> 00:04:53.893
Before he could finish, Cole hurried over to Henry.

70
00:04:53.894 --> 00:04:59.589
"Excuse us," Cole said to Rebecca. Then he pulled Henry away.

71
00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:03.163
"That's not where Daisy's shirt was hanging!" he whispered.

72
00:05:03.164 --> 00:05:08.347
"Yes, it was," Henry said. "That's Daisy's pony right there.

73
00:05:08.348 --> 00:05:13.950
Her show coat was hanging there too, until she put it on for her last class."

74
00:05:13.951 --> 00:05:15.785
Cole looked confused.

75
00:05:15.786 --> 00:05:21.076
"It was? But I saw Daisy's shirt hanging on that stall over there."

76
00:05:21.077 --> 00:05:24.079
Cole pointed to the stall next to Big Spot's.

77
00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:27.379
Kira's pony was standing there, looking out.

78
00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:31.033
Henry looked at Kira's pony, and then slowly he smiled.

79
00:05:31.034 --> 00:05:34.655
"Let's go find Daisy," he told Cole.

80
00:05:34.656 --> 00:05:40.297
"I think I know exactly what happened to her shirt."
